@startuml
left to right direction
actor "DMS Viewer" as Viewer
rectangle "APGC DMS — read-only access" {
  usecase "View explicitly granted Memo\n[CURRENT: DocumentAccess.can_view]" as View
  usecase "Search visible references / titles\n[CURRENT: Memo list only]" as Search
  usecase "View available versions / activity\n[CURRENT: visible detail]" as History
  usecase "Preview finalized PDF / supported attachment\n[CURRENT: state + visibility]" as Preview
  usecase "Download\n[CURRENT: owner or can_view + can_download]" as Download
  usecase "Create / edit / decide / finalize / archive\n[FUTURE: explicitly denied by Viewer policy]" as Mutate
  usecase "Assigned workflow decision\n[CURRENT: assignment overrides role label]" as Task
}
Viewer --> View
Viewer --> Search
Viewer --> History
Viewer --> Preview
Viewer --> Download
Viewer ..> Mutate : target read-only boundary
Viewer --> Task
note bottom of Task
  Viewer membership does not currently enforce read-only.
  If the user is assigned a pending task, the application
  currently allows that task decision regardless of role.
end note
@enduml
